{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 515890, "name": "Vlad Didenko", "username": "vldid", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vldid/{size}/55999_2.png", "created_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:31.133Z", "cooked": "<p>Making an image, with this in the beginning:</p>\n<pre><code>FROM registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora-minimal:44\n\nCOPY dnf.conf /etc/dnf/dnf.conf\n\nRUN dnf --assumeyes \\\n        install \\\n        curl ffmpeg git ripgrep tar xz\n</code></pre>\n<p>The <code>dnf.conf</code> is:</p>\n<pre><code>[main]\ngpgcheck=1\nclean_requirements_on_remove=True\ninstall_weak_deps=False\ntsflags=nodocs\n</code></pre>\n<p>Dependencies should be fairly small:</p>\n<pre><code>$ dnf repoquery --depends curl ffmpeg git ripgrep tar xz | wc -l\nUpdating and loading repositories:\nRepositories loaded.\n47\n</code></pre>\n<p>Definitely nothing which should pull in the whole Wayland and parts of Gnome.</p>\n<p>Yet, when <code>podman build</code> runs it on Fedora 44 Workstation, it does, pulls a bunch of GUI and other auxiliary packages (331 total). I can’t seem to be able to figure out what triggers it.</p>\n<p>What is a way to limit the <code>dnf install</code> scope?</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 4, "updated_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:31.133Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 10, "reads": 39, "readers_count": 38, "score": 62.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 196178, "topic_slug": "unexpected-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Vlad Didenko", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34510, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unexpected-unneeded-packages/196178/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 515894, "name": "Villy Kruse", "username": "vekruse", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/v/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-07-08T04:46:20.339Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"vldid\" data-display-name=\"Vlad Didenko\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"196178\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vldid/48/55999_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Vlad Didenko:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yet, when <code>podman build</code> runs it on Fedora 44 Workstation, it does, pulls a bunch of GUI and other auxiliary packages (331 total). I can’t seem to be able to figure out what triggers it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The ffmeg does requires a bunch of gui stuff, and that can be satisfied by different set of packages.  If you don’t specify the desktop environment, it is a bit arbitrary which gui packages will be included to satisfy the requirements.  If you don’t want any gui stuff, then leave out the ffmpeg package.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 4, "updated_at": "2026-07-08T04:46:20.339Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 35, "readers_count": 34, "score": 42.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 196178, "topic_slug": "unexpected-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Villy Kruse", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 8762, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unexpected-unneeded-packages/196178/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 516032, "name": "Vlad Didenko", "username": "vldid", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vldid/{size}/55999_2.png", "created_at": "2026-07-08T20:24:40.603Z", "cooked": "<p>Removing <code>ffmpeg</code> from the command reduces the list indeed. It is required in this project, though, so other things start to break.</p>\n<p>A couple follow-up questions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Where do you see the dependencies? The query returns none:</li>\n</ol>\n<pre data-code-wrap=\"bash\"><code class=\"lang-bash\">    $ dnf repoquery --depends ffmpeg | wc -l\n    Updating and loading repositories:\n    Repositories loaded.\n    0\n</code></pre>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>This is for a minimal and lightweight container to run an agent, which requires <code>ffmpeg</code> for processing visuals. How do people deal with that bloat if <code>ffpmeg</code> is needed in an image?</li>\n</ol>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 4, "updated_at": "2026-07-08T20:29:42.862Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 13.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 196178, "topic_slug": "unexpected-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Vlad Didenko", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 8762, "username": "vekruse", "name": "Villy Kruse", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/v/aad0ee/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34510, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unexpected-unneeded-packages/196178/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 516094, "name": "Vlad Didenko", "username": "vldid", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vldid/{size}/55999_2.png", "created_at": "2026-07-09T04:48:04.770Z", "cooked": "<p>Well, the correct dependency chain starts with <code>sdl2-compat</code>, and branches from there. The reason it was not visible on the <code>ffmpeg</code> package is because it is actually <code>ffmpeg-free</code> package, and <code>dnf</code> completely obfuscates the fact, so annoying.</p>\n<p>I did not find a way for decline this crazy dependency tree. For now I am sourcing <a href=\"http://ffmpeg.org\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">ffmpeg.org</a>’s <a href=\"https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases\">pre-build static binaries</a> to get around this nasty. But will think hard to pick another setup (maybe not Fedora) for the next project.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 4, "updated_at": "2026-07-09T04:48:04.770Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 16, "readers_count": 15, "score": 3.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 196178, "topic_slug": "unexpected-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Vlad Didenko", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Releases · BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds · GitHub", "clicks": 0}, {"url": "http://ffmpeg.org", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "FFmpeg", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 34510, "username": "vldid", "name": "Vlad Didenko", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vldid/{size}/55999_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34510, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unexpected-unneeded-packages/196178/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": true, "topic_accepted_answer": true}], "stream": [515890, 515894, 516032, 516094]}, "timeline_lookup": [[1, 119], [3, 118]], "suggested_topics": [], "tags": [{"id": 1438, "name": "f44", "slug": "f44"}, {"id": 